# RaktSetu — one OPTIONAL environment variable, and no secrets.
#
# The data layer is a local SQLite file. There is no database URL, no API key and
# no connection string to supply, because nothing talks to a network service.
#
# RAKTSETU_DATA_DIR
#   Directory that holds `raktsetu.db`. In production it must be a PERSISTENT,
#   WRITABLE VOLUME that survives restarts and deploys (the container uses
#   `/data`; the Render blueprint mounts its disk there). Unset, it defaults to
#   `./data` beside the app, which is correct for local development.
#
#   Nothing else in the application reads configuration. `src/lib/server/db.ts`
#   is the only file permitted to read `process.env`, and this is the only
#   variable it reads — `npm run check:invariants` enforces both facts. The
#   session cookie's `Secure` flag is still derived from the request's own
#   protocol rather than from an environment variable.
#
# A .env.local left over from an earlier cloud-based build is harmless: none of
# the variables such a file would contain are read any more.

